{"name":"Adúnaic","sort":10000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-adunaic","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-adunaic","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Adûnaïque","pages":[{"name":"Adûnaïque","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Adûnaïque</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien / développé par ICE pour le jeu</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Númenóréens et de leurs descendants. Le corpus MERP la présente comme l’ancienne langue des Dúnedain de Númenor, apparentée aux langues des Hommes du Nord et devenue l’un des principaux ancêtres du Westron. Au Troisième Âge, elle survit surtout dans les milieux dúnedain cultivés, notamment au Gondor et parmi les héritiers de Númenor. Elle est prestigieuse mais rarement employée comme langue quotidienne.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Adúnaic","pages":[{"name":"Adúnaic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Adúnaic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / expanded by ICE for play</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Númenóreans and their descendants. MERP presents it as the old tongue of the Dúnedain of Númenor, related to the Northman languages and one of the principal ancestors of Westron. In the Third Age it survives chiefly among learned Dúnedain, especially in Gondor and among the heirs of Númenor. It is prestigious but seldom an everyday language.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Adúnaic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Adúnaic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / expanded by ICE for play</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Númenóreans and their descendants. MERP presents it as the old tongue of the Dúnedain of Númenor, related to the Northman languages and one of the principal ancestors of Westron. In the Third Age it survives chiefly among learned Dúnedain, especially in Gondor and among the heirs of Númenor. It is prestigious but seldom an everyday language.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"9kzF8ehs0V4IcLtw"}
{"name":"Ansith","sort":20000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-ansith","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-ansith","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Ansith","pages":[{"name":"Ansith","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Ansith</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue associée dans MERP aux peuples du sud et de l’est rencontrés dans les cultures Rijeshnarod et Narodbrijig. La compilation utilisée par MERP-RMU l’emploie comme langue secondaire de plusieurs groupes apysani, mais ne fournit pas, dans son répertoire linguistique principal, de description historique ou grammaticale détaillée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Ansith","pages":[{"name":"Ansith","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Ansith</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A language associated in MERP with southern and eastern peoples, notably the Rijeshnarod and Narodbrijig cultures. The compilation used by MERP-RMU treats it as a secondary language among several Apysani groups, but its main language survey gives no detailed historical or grammatical account.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Ansith","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Ansith</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A language associated in MERP with southern and eastern peoples, notably the Rijeshnarod and Narodbrijig cultures. The compilation used by MERP-RMU treats it as a secondary language among several Apysani groups, but its main language survey gives no detailed historical or grammatical account.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"C6x0VdodOtGYwtIL"}
{"name":"Apysaic","sort":30000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-apysaic","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-apysaic","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Apysaïque","pages":[{"name":"Apysaïque","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Apysaïque</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Grande famille linguistique du sud-ouest d’Endor, associée aux peuples apysani et aux Haradrim méridionaux. MERP distingue plusieurs vagues migratoires et des formes septentrionales plus tardives fortement influencées par le Haradaic. C’est donc moins une langue parfaitement uniforme qu’un ensemble de parlers apparentés.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Apysaic","pages":[{"name":"Apysaic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Apysaic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A major language family of south-western Endor, associated with the Apysani peoples and southern Haradrim. MERP distinguishes several migration waves and later northern forms strongly influenced by Haradaic. It is therefore better understood as a family of related speech forms than as one perfectly uniform language.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Apysaic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Apysaic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A major language family of south-western Endor, associated with the Apysani peoples and southern Haradrim. MERP distinguishes several migration waves and later northern forms strongly influenced by Haradaic. It is therefore better understood as a family of related speech forms than as one perfectly uniform language.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"2GLOjAYAnfVueWsP"}
{"name":"Atliduk","sort":40000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-atliduk","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-atliduk","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Atliduk","pages":[{"name":"Atliduk","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Atliduk</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Béornides, appelée Beijabar dans les sources ICE. Elle dérive d’anciens parlers des Hommes du Nord d’Eriador. Dans MERP-RMU, elle représente la langue vernaculaire traditionnelle des Béornides, distincte du Westron qu’ils utilisent également.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Beorning culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Atliduk","pages":[{"name":"Atliduk","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Atliduk</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Beornings, called Beijabar in ICE sources. It derives from ancient Northman speech of Eriador. In MERP-RMU it represents the traditional vernacular of the Beornings, distinct from the Westron they also use.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Beorning culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Atliduk","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Atliduk</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Beornings, called Beijabar in ICE sources. It derives from ancient Northman speech of Eriador. In MERP-RMU it represents the traditional vernacular of the Beornings, distinct from the Westron they also use.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Beorning culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"XBacx44DbyZnkK6U"}
{"name":"Bethteur","sort":50000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-bethteur","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-bethteur","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Bethteur","pages":[{"name":"Bethteur","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Bethteur</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue elfique sylvaine employée dans la Forêt Noire selon le corpus MERP. Elle est associée aux Elfes sylvains et aux Nandor et appartient au vaste ensemble des parlers avarins et sylvains développés par ICE pour représenter la diversité des communautés elfiques orientales.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Elven cultures</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Bethteur","pages":[{"name":"Bethteur","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Bethteur</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Silvan Elvish language used in Mirkwood according to MERP. It is associated with Silvan Elves and Nandor and belongs to the wider set of Avarin/Silvan tongues developed by ICE to represent the diversity of eastern Elvish communities.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Elven cultures</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Bethteur","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Bethteur</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Silvan Elvish language used in Mirkwood according to MERP. It is associated with Silvan Elves and Nandor and belongs to the wider set of Avarin/Silvan tongues developed by ICE to represent the diversity of eastern Elvish communities.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Elven cultures</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"dz6pRjx5IgYgThUN"}
{"name":"Black Speech","sort":60000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-black-speech","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-black-speech","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Parler Noir","pages":[{"name":"Parler Noir","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Parler Noir</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien / compléments MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Le Parler Noir fut créé par Sauron comme langue de domination pour ses serviteurs. MERP distingue une forme relativement pure, réservée surtout aux plus hauts serviteurs du Seigneur Ténébreux, et de nombreux dialectes dégradés employés par les Orcs. Sa sonorité est volontairement dure et heurtée. L’inscription de l’Anneau Unique en est l’exemple le plus célèbre.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — The Lord of the Rings artwork</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Black Speech","pages":[{"name":"Black Speech","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Black Speech</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP additions</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The Black Speech was devised by Sauron as a language of domination for his servants. MERP distinguishes a relatively pure form, chiefly used by the higher servants of the Dark Lord, from many debased dialects spoken by Orcs. Its sound is deliberately harsh and clashing. The inscription on the One Ring is its most famous example.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — The Lord of the Rings artwork</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Black Speech","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Black Speech</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP additions</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The Black Speech was devised by Sauron as a language of domination for his servants. MERP distinguishes a relatively pure form, chiefly used by the higher servants of the Dark Lord, from many debased dialects spoken by Orcs. Its sound is deliberately harsh and clashing. The inscription on the One Ring is its most famous example.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — The Lord of the Rings artwork</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"8YXKS94uUftjebfr"}
{"name":"Blarm","sort":70000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-blarm","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-blarm","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Blarm","pages":[{"name":"Blarm","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Blarm</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Hommes des Collines de Rhudaur. Les sources MERP la présentent comme le parler traditionnel de ces communautés, souvent employé aux côtés du Westron. Le corpus disponible donne peu de détails supplémentaires sur son écriture ou sa structure.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Hillmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Blarm","pages":[{"name":"Blarm","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Blarm</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The tongue of the Hillmen of Rhudaur. MERP presents it as the traditional speech of these communities, often used alongside Westron. The available corpus gives little further detail on its writing or structure.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Hillmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Blarm","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Blarm</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The tongue of the Hillmen of Rhudaur. MERP presents it as the traditional speech of these communities, often used alongside Westron. The available corpus gives little further detail on its writing or structure.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Hillmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"O7cVbgKL0Z7P4YVj"}
{"name":"Cuindî","sort":80000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-cuindi","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-cuindi","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Cuindî","pages":[{"name":"Cuindî","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Cuindî</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue elfique avarine ou sylvaine associée aux Fuinar dans les cultures MERP. Elle appartient aux nombreux parlers elfiques orientaux créés ou développés par ICE pour les régions éloignées des grands centres sindarins et noldorins. Les sources utilisées par MERP-RMU n’en donnent pas de grammaire détaillée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Fuinar culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Cuindî","pages":[{"name":"Cuindî","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Cuindî</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>An Avarin/Silvan Elvish tongue associated with the Fuinar in MERP cultures. It belongs to the many eastern Elvish speech forms created or expanded by ICE for regions far from the Sindarin and Noldorin centres. The sources used by MERP-RMU provide no detailed grammar.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Fuinar culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Cuindî","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Cuindî</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>An Avarin/Silvan Elvish tongue associated with the Fuinar in MERP cultures. It belongs to the many eastern Elvish speech forms created or expanded by ICE for regions far from the Sindarin and Noldorin centres. The sources used by MERP-RMU provide no detailed grammar.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Fuinar culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"fopUC7NJnUYN10rp"}
{"name":"Debased Labba","sort":90000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-debased-labba","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-debased-labba","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Labba dégradé","pages":[{"name":"Labba dégradé","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Labba dégradé</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Variante MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Forme dégradée du Labba employée par certains Trolls des Neiges. Elle ne constitue pas une langue savante autonome : MERP l’utilise pour représenter un parler fortement simplifié, limité et altéré par rapport à la langue des Lossoth.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Snow Troll culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP Labba entry</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Debased Labba","pages":[{"name":"Debased Labba","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Debased Labba</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP variant</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A debased form of Labba used by some Snow Trolls. It is not a separate learned language: MERP uses it to represent heavily simplified and altered speech derived from the tongue of the Lossoth.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Snow Troll culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP Labba entry</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Debased Labba","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Debased Labba</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP variant</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A debased form of Labba used by some Snow Trolls. It is not a separate learned language: MERP uses it to represent heavily simplified and altered speech derived from the tongue of the Lossoth.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Snow Troll culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP Labba entry</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"WAJCcTZDPO7DQrhK"}
{"name":"Debased Westron","sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-debased-westron","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-debased-westron","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Westron dégradé","pages":[{"name":"Westron dégradé","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Westron dégradé</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Variante MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Forme rudimentaire et dégradée du Westron employée par plusieurs populations trolles. Elle permet une communication élémentaire sans offrir la richesse, la précision ni les usages sociaux du parler commun des peuples libres.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Troll cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP Westron entry</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Debased Westron","pages":[{"name":"Debased Westron","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Debased Westron</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP variant</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A rudimentary and debased form of Westron used by several Troll populations. It allows elementary communication but lacks the richness, precision, and social range of the Common Speech used by the Free Peoples.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Troll cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP Westron entry</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Debased Westron","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Debased Westron</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP variant</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A rudimentary and debased form of Westron used by several Troll populations. It allows elementary communication but lacks the richness, precision, and social range of the Common Speech used by the Free Peoples.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Troll cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP Westron entry</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"op2O3Cg3jdjAYXBt"}
{"name":"Drel","sort":110000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-drel","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-drel","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Drel","pages":[{"name":"Drel","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Drel</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue méridionale associée aux Fuinar et à certains peuples d’Endor dans les développements ICE. Dans MERP-RMU, elle apparaît comme langue culturelle secondaire. La compilation de référence ne lui consacre pas de notice linguistique détaillée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Fuinar culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Drel","pages":[{"name":"Drel","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Drel</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A southern language associated with the Fuinar and other peoples of Endor in ICE developments. In MERP-RMU it appears as a secondary cultural language. The reference compilation does not provide a detailed linguistic entry for it.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Fuinar culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Drel","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Drel</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A southern language associated with the Fuinar and other peoples of Endor in ICE developments. In MERP-RMU it appears as a secondary cultural language. The reference compilation does not provide a detailed linguistic entry for it.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Fuinar culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"ZtzzOMPqIvzgGTTu"}
{"name":"Dunael","sort":120000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-dunael","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-dunael","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Dunael","pages":[{"name":"Dunael","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Dunael</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP à partir du légendaire</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Dunlendings. MERP insiste sur son caractère distinct des langues des Hommes du Nord et des héritiers des Edain. La tradition orale y occupe une place majeure : l’écrit est relativement rare et l’éloquence, la mémoire et les arts de la parole sont particulièrement valorisés.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Daen Lintis culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Dunael","pages":[{"name":"Dunael","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Dunael</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP development from the legendarium</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Dunlendings. MERP stresses that it is distinct from the languages of the Northmen and the heirs of the Edain. Oral tradition is especially important: writing is relatively rare, while eloquence, memory, and performance are highly valued.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Daen Lintis culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Dunael","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Dunael</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP development from the legendarium</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Dunlendings. MERP stresses that it is distinct from the languages of the Northmen and the heirs of the Edain. Oral tradition is especially important: writing is relatively rare, while eloquence, memory, and performance are highly valued.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Daen Lintis culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"kAuRQqHb8mykyIun"}
{"name":"Gramuik","sort":130000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-gramuik","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-gramuik","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Gramuik","pages":[{"name":"Gramuik","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Gramuik</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Dialecte du Rhovanion employé par les Gramuz. Il appartient au continuum des langues des Hommes du Nord et coexiste fréquemment avec le Westron. Les sources MERP-RMU l’utilisent surtout pour caractériser l’identité culturelle et régionale des Gramuz.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Gramuz culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Gramuik","pages":[{"name":"Gramuik","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Gramuik</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Rhovanion dialect used by the Gramuz. It belongs to the Northman linguistic continuum and often coexists with Westron. MERP-RMU chiefly uses it to express the regional and cultural identity of the Gramuz.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Gramuz culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Gramuik","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Gramuik</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Rhovanion dialect used by the Gramuz. It belongs to the Northman linguistic continuum and often coexists with Westron. MERP-RMU chiefly uses it to express the regional and cultural identity of the Gramuz.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Gramuz culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"DZNA7t9QAVttf1Dj"}
{"name":"Haradaic","sort":140000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-haradaic","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-haradaic","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Haradaïque","pages":[{"name":"Haradaïque","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Haradaïque</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Haradrim septentrionaux. Elle est l’un des grands parlers du Harad et exerce une influence notable sur certaines formes septentrionales de l’Apysaic. Elle sert aussi de langue de contact dans plusieurs cultures méridionales.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Harad cultures</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Haradaic","pages":[{"name":"Haradaic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Haradaic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the northern Haradrim. It is one of the major tongues of Harad and strongly influences some northern forms of Apysaic. It also serves as a contact language among several southern cultures.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Harad cultures</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Haradaic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Haradaic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the northern Haradrim. It is one of the major tongues of Harad and strongly influences some northern forms of Apysaic. It also serves as a contact language among several southern cultures.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Harad cultures</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"qffs7FXt6LDUjpnu"}
{"name":"Honnin","sort":150000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-honnin","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-honnin","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Honnin","pages":[{"name":"Honnin","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Honnin</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue propre aux Honnin/Suzamatu dans le matériel MERP. La Culture Honnin l’emploie essentiellement comme langue parlée et ne lui attribue pas de tradition écrite ordinaire. Les sources utilisées ici ne fournissent pas de description grammaticale plus complète.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Honnin culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Honnin","pages":[{"name":"Honnin","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Honnin</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Honnin/Suzamatu in MERP material. The Honnin culture treats it primarily as a spoken language with no ordinary written tradition. The sources used here provide no fuller grammatical description.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Honnin culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Honnin","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Honnin</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Honnin/Suzamatu in MERP material. The Honnin culture treats it primarily as a spoken language with no ordinary written tradition. The sources used here provide no fuller grammatical description.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Honnin culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"3ITznskil0AYqZ1U"}
{"name":"Khuzdul","sort":160000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-khuzdul","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-khuzdul","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Khuzdul","pages":[{"name":"Khuzdul","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Khuzdul</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien / compléments MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue secrète des Khazâd, traditionnellement peu enseignée aux étrangers. MERP la décrit comme une langue de savoir et de haute parole, à la sonorité gutturale, structurée autour de racines consonantiques. Son écriture traditionnelle utilise les Cirth, notamment l’Angerthas Moria. Les Nains emploient volontiers le Westron ou les langues locales lorsqu’ils s’adressent aux autres peuples.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Khuzdul","pages":[{"name":"Khuzdul","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Khuzdul</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP additions</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The secret language of the Khazâd, traditionally taught to very few outsiders. MERP describes it as a language of lore and high speech, with a guttural sound and a structure built around consonantal roots. Its traditional writing uses the Cirth, notably the Angerthas Moria. Dwarves readily use Westron or local languages when speaking with other peoples.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Khuzdul","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Khuzdul</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP additions</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The secret language of the Khazâd, traditionally taught to very few outsiders. MERP describes it as a language of lore and high speech, with a guttural sound and a structure built around consonantal roots. Its traditional writing uses the Cirth, notably the Angerthas Moria. Dwarves readily use Westron or local languages when speaking with other peoples.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"5BxG7DFWUWpayz9P"}
{"name":"Kuorith","sort":170000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-kuorith","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-kuorith","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Kuorith","pages":[{"name":"Kuorith","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Kuorith</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue principale des Kuorind/Ûshasai dans les cultures MERP. Elle est présentée comme une langue pleinement parlée et écrite, employée parallèlement au Lynerian. Le répertoire linguistique des pages 218–219 ne lui consacre pas de notice séparée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Kuorind culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Kuorith","pages":[{"name":"Kuorith","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Kuorith</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The principal language of the Kuorind/Ûshasai in MERP cultures. It is presented as a fully spoken and written language used alongside Lynerian. The language survey on pp. 218–219 does not provide a separate detailed entry.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Kuorind culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Kuorith","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Kuorith</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The principal language of the Kuorind/Ûshasai in MERP cultures. It is presented as a fully spoken and written language used alongside Lynerian. The language survey on pp. 218–219 does not provide a separate detailed entry.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Kuorind culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"NY6qYS0RmoP5rX9V"}
{"name":"Labba","sort":180000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-labba","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-labba","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Labba","pages":[{"name":"Labba","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Labba</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Lossoth, issue dans MERP d’une branche mornerine dite Aravadorin. Elle est fortement façonnée par l’environnement arctique : le vocabulaire relatif à la neige, à la glace et aux conditions du nord est particulièrement développé. Les sources MERP précisent qu’elle ne possède pas de forme écrite.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Lossoth culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Labba","pages":[{"name":"Labba","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Labba</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Lossoth, derived in MERP from the Mornerin Aravadorin branch. It is strongly shaped by the Arctic environment: vocabulary relating to snow, ice, and northern conditions is especially rich. MERP explicitly states that it has no written form.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Lossoth culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Labba","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Labba</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Lossoth, derived in MERP from the Mornerin Aravadorin branch. It is strongly shaped by the Arctic environment: vocabulary relating to snow, ice, and northern conditions is especially rich. MERP explicitly states that it has no written form.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Lossoth culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"lHCmse3DrcUUNDc9"}
{"name":"Logathig","sort":190000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-logathig","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-logathig","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Logathig","pages":[{"name":"Logathig","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Logathig</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue associée aux Dorwinrim et à plusieurs peuples orientaux. Elle sert de grand parler régional dans une partie du Rhovanion oriental et des territoires voisins. MERP-RMU la rencontre notamment chez les Dorwinrim, les Orientaux et certains Hommes du Nord urbanisés.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Logathig","pages":[{"name":"Logathig","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Logathig</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A language associated with the Dorwinrim and several eastern peoples. It functions as a major regional tongue across parts of eastern Rhovanion and neighbouring lands. MERP-RMU encounters it among Dorwinrim, Easterlings, and some Urban Northmen.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Logathig","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Logathig</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A language associated with the Dorwinrim and several eastern peoples. It functions as a major regional tongue across parts of eastern Rhovanion and neighbouring lands. MERP-RMU encounters it among Dorwinrim, Easterlings, and some Urban Northmen.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP culture descriptions</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"rji1Sc94oPGX5KBt"}
{"name":"Luinbeth","sort":200000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-luinbeth","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-luinbeth","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Luinbeth","pages":[{"name":"Luinbeth","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Luinbeth</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Luindrim/Foredhil-Iaurwaith dans le matériel MERP. Elle est décrite par leur Culture comme une langue maîtrisée à un niveau très élevé, aux côtés du Sindarin. Les sources disponibles ici n’en détaillent pas davantage la parenté linguistique.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Luindrim culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Luinbeth","pages":[{"name":"Luinbeth","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Luinbeth</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Luindrim/Foredhil-Iaurwaith in MERP material. Their culture treats it as a highly developed native language used alongside Sindarin. The sources available here do not further define its linguistic relationships.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Luindrim culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Luinbeth","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Luinbeth</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Luindrim/Foredhil-Iaurwaith in MERP material. Their culture treats it as a highly developed native language used alongside Sindarin. The sources available here do not further define its linguistic relationships.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Luindrim culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"A0QffRzibF6XatWn"}
{"name":"Lynerian","sort":210000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-lynerian","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-lynerian","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Lynerian","pages":[{"name":"Lynerian","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Lynerian</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue régionale d’Endor oriental ou méridional employée notamment par les Kuorind et les Pêdi dans le matériel MERP. Elle possède des usages parlés et écrits complets dans ces cultures, mais la compilation de référence ne lui fournit pas de notice historique détaillée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Kuorind and Pêdi cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Lynerian","pages":[{"name":"Lynerian","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Lynerian</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A regional language of eastern or southern Endor used notably by the Kuorind and Pêdi in MERP material. It has full spoken and written use in those cultures, but the reference compilation provides no detailed historical entry.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Kuorind and Pêdi cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Lynerian","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Lynerian</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A regional language of eastern or southern Endor used notably by the Kuorind and Pêdi in MERP material. It has full spoken and written use in those cultures, but the reference compilation provides no detailed historical entry.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Kuorind and Pêdi cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"Pi6mgHACS7O1W6da"}
{"name":"Nahaiduk","sort":220000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-nahaiduk","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-nahaiduk","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Nahaiduk","pages":[{"name":"Nahaiduk","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Nahaiduk</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Dialecte des Hommes du Nord du Rhovanion associé particulièrement aux Hommes des Bois. Il appartient à la même vaste sphère linguistique que d’autres parlers nordiques et coexiste souvent avec le Westron.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Woodmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Nahaiduk","pages":[{"name":"Nahaiduk","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Nahaiduk</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Rhovanion Northman dialect especially associated with the Woodmen. It belongs to the same broad linguistic sphere as other northern tongues and often coexists with Westron.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Woodmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Nahaiduk","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Nahaiduk</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Rhovanion Northman dialect especially associated with the Woodmen. It belongs to the same broad linguistic sphere as other northern tongues and often coexists with Westron.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Woodmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"aF1iN6XOlfi5O4wV"}
{"name":"Orkish","sort":230000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-orkish","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-orkish","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Orc","pages":[{"name":"Orc","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Orc</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien / systématisation MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>« Orcien » désigne moins une langue unique qu’un ensemble de parlers tribaux. MERP insiste sur leur vocabulaire commun de jurons et d’injures et sur leur forte dépendance à des dialectes fondés sur le Westron, le Parler Noir ou parfois des langues méridionales. Deux tribus orques peuvent ainsi éprouver de réelles difficultés à se comprendre.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Orkish","pages":[{"name":"Orkish","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Orkish</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP systematisation</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>“Orkish” is less a single language than a collection of tribal speech forms. MERP stresses their shared stock of curses and insults and their strong dependence on dialects based on Westron, the Black Speech, or occasionally southern languages. Two Orc tribes may therefore have genuine difficulty understanding one another.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Orkish","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Orkish</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP systematisation</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>“Orkish” is less a single language than a collection of tribal speech forms. MERP stresses their shared stock of curses and insults and their strong dependence on dialects based on Westron, the Black Speech, or occasionally southern languages. Two Orc tribes may therefore have genuine difficulty understanding one another.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"dPMtKvDfpypOfWTy"}
{"name":"Pêdu","sort":240000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-pedu","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-pedu","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Pêdu","pages":[{"name":"Pêdu","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Pêdu</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Pêdi/Jashcâi dans les cultures MERP, utilisée comme langue native pleinement développée et écrite. Elle est pratiquée parallèlement au Lynerian. La compilation de référence l’énumère parmi les langues d’Endor sans fournir une notice historique détaillée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Pêdi culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Pêdu","pages":[{"name":"Pêdu","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Pêdu</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Pêdi/Jashcâi in MERP cultures, used as a fully developed native written language. It is practised alongside Lynerian. The reference compilation lists it among the languages of Endor without providing a detailed historical entry.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Pêdi culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Pêdu","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Pêdu</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Pêdi/Jashcâi in MERP cultures, used as a fully developed native written language. It is practised alongside Lynerian. The reference compilation lists it among the languages of Endor without providing a detailed historical entry.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Pêdi culture</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"0bX6WbF1nRln0IKr"}
{"name":"Pûkael","sort":250000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-pukael","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-pukael","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Pûkael","pages":[{"name":"Pûkael","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Pûkael</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP à partir des Drúedain</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue gutturale des Woses/Drúedain, présentée comme très différente des autres langues humaines. MERP en fait l’ancêtre du Daenael puis, indirectement, du Dunael et de plusieurs anciens parlers côtiers. Les Woses utilisent des pictogrammes simples plutôt qu’une écriture alphabétique traditionnelle, notamment pour marquer les chemins et transmettre des signaux.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Drughu culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Pûkael","pages":[{"name":"Pûkael","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Pûkael</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP development from the Drúedain</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The guttural language of the Woses/Drúedain, presented as very different from other Mannish tongues. MERP makes it the ancestor of Daenael and, indirectly, Dunael and several ancient coastal languages. The Woses use simple pictograms rather than a conventional alphabetic script, notably to mark paths and signal one another.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Drughu culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Pûkael","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Pûkael</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP development from the Drúedain</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The guttural language of the Woses/Drúedain, presented as very different from other Mannish tongues. MERP makes it the ancestor of Daenael and, indirectly, Dunael and several ancient coastal languages. The Woses use simple pictograms rather than a conventional alphabetic script, notably to mark paths and signal one another.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Drughu culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"YhMTnfSMynqTYXaT"}
{"name":"Quenya","sort":260000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-quenya","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-quenya","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Quenya","pages":[{"name":"Quenya","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Quenya</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Le Haut-Elfique est, avec le Sindarin, l’une des deux principales langues elfiques du légendaire. Au Troisième Âge, son usage quotidien en Terre du Milieu est limité ; il demeure une langue de savoir, de mémoire, de cérémonie et de haute culture, particulièrement importante chez les Noldor. Les Tengwar de Fëanor furent à l’origine conçus pour écrire le Quenya.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Tolkien’s Invented Languages</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Quenya","pages":[{"name":"Quenya","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Quenya</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>High-elven is, together with Sindarin, one of the two chief Elvish languages of the legendarium. In the Third Age its everyday use in Middle-earth is limited; it remains a language of lore, memory, ceremony, and high culture, especially important among the Noldor. The Tengwar of Fëanor were originally devised to write Quenya.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Tolkien’s Invented Languages</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Quenya","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Quenya</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>High-elven is, together with Sindarin, one of the two chief Elvish languages of the legendarium. In the Third Age its everyday use in Middle-earth is limited; it remains a language of lore, memory, ceremony, and high culture, especially important among the Noldor. The Tengwar of Fëanor were originally devised to write Quenya.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Tolkien’s Invented Languages</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"k6Iv6ktHzksbzmez"}
{"name":"Rhovaik","sort":270000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-rhovaik","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-rhovaik","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Rhovaik","pages":[{"name":"Rhovaik","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Rhovaik</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Dialecte des Hommes du Nord du Rhovanion, associé aux populations de Dale et d’Esgaroth et, dans MERP, aux Hommes du Nord urbanisés. Il représente une branche plus citadine des parlers nordiques.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Urban Northmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Rhovaik","pages":[{"name":"Rhovaik","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Rhovaik</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Rhovanion Northman dialect associated with the peoples of Dale and Esgaroth and, in MERP, with Urban Northmen. It represents a more urban branch of the northern speech continuum.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Urban Northmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Rhovaik","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Rhovaik</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A Rhovanion Northman dialect associated with the peoples of Dale and Esgaroth and, in MERP, with Urban Northmen. It represents a more urban branch of the northern speech continuum.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Urban Northmen culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"MfXEo9H6iF3UkkyP"}
{"name":"Rohirric","sort":280000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-rohirric","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-rohirric","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Rohirrique","pages":[{"name":"Rohirrique","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Rohirrique</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien / systématisation MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Rohirrim, issue des anciens parlers des Hommes du Nord. MERP la présente comme une langue conservatrice, affinée dans les hautes vallées de l’Anduin puis maintenue au Rohan après l’installation des Éothéod. Elle demeure distincte du Westron, même si la plupart des Rohirrim connaissent également le parler commun.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Rohirrim culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Rohirric","pages":[{"name":"Rohirric","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Rohirric</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP systematisation</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Rohirrim, descended from older Northman speech. MERP presents it as conservative, refined in the upper Vales of Anduin and maintained in Rohan after the settlement of the Éothéod. It remains distinct from Westron, although most Rohirrim also know the Common Speech.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Rohirrim culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Rohirric","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Rohirric</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP systematisation</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Rohirrim, descended from older Northman speech. MERP presents it as conservative, refined in the upper Vales of Anduin and maintained in Rohan after the settlement of the Éothéod. It remains distinct from Westron, although most Rohirrim also know the Common Speech.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Rohirrim culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"rFtRiWQTvUQrmFoW"}
{"name":"Silvan","sort":290000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-silvan","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-silvan","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Sylvain","pages":[{"name":"Sylvain","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Sylvain</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Terme utilisé dans MERP-RMU pour certains parlers des Elfes sylvains. Il ne désigne pas nécessairement une langue unique et uniforme : les traditions sylvaines couvrent plusieurs communautés, souvent en contact avec le Sindarin et d’autres langues elfiques orientales.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>MERP Elven cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Silvan","pages":[{"name":"Silvan","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Silvan</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A term used in MERP-RMU for some forms of Silvan Elvish speech. It need not denote a single uniform language: Silvan traditions encompass several communities, often in contact with Sindarin and other eastern Elvish tongues.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Elven cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Silvan","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Silvan</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A term used in MERP-RMU for some forms of Silvan Elvish speech. It need not denote a single uniform language: Silvan traditions encompass several communities, often in contact with Sindarin and other eastern Elvish tongues.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>MERP Elven cultures</li><li>RMSS/RMFRP language abbreviations</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"o4tpHd8gowmLkBW5"}
{"name":"Sindarin","sort":300000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-sindarin","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-sindarin","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Sindarin","pages":[{"name":"Sindarin","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Sindarin</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Le Gris-Elfique est, avec le Quenya, l’une des deux grandes langues elfiques du légendaire. Il devient la principale langue elfique de communication en Terre du Milieu et exerce une forte influence sur les langues et noms des Dúnedain. Les Cirth furent inventées par les Elfes sindarins de Beleriand ; l’Angerthas Daeron en constitue la forme runique la plus développée.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Tolkien’s Invented Languages</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Sindarin","pages":[{"name":"Sindarin","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Sindarin</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>Grey-elven is, together with Quenya, one of the two chief Elvish languages of the legendarium. It becomes the principal Elvish language of communication in Middle-earth and strongly influences Dúnedain speech and naming. The Cirth were invented by the Sindarin Elves of Beleriand; the Angerthas Daeron is their most developed runic form.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Tolkien’s Invented Languages</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Sindarin","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Sindarin</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>Grey-elven is, together with Quenya, one of the two chief Elvish languages of the legendarium. It becomes the principal Elvish language of communication in Middle-earth and strongly influences Dúnedain speech and naming. The Cirth were invented by the Sindarin Elves of Beleriand; the Angerthas Daeron is their most developed runic form.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Tolkien’s Invented Languages</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Writing Systems</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"KlRDE8NhJRNiuJ3X"}
{"name":"Umitic","sort":310000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-umitic","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-umitic","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Umitique","pages":[{"name":"Umitique","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Umitique</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Umli. Dans MERP, elle constitue leur parler culturel principal et coexiste avec le Labba, le Westron et parfois le Khuzdul. Les sources utilisées par MERP-RMU n’en fournissent pas de description historique détaillée au-delà de cette association.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Umli culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Umitic","pages":[{"name":"Umitic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Umitic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Umli. In MERP it is their principal cultural tongue and coexists with Labba, Westron, and sometimes Khuzdul. The sources used by MERP-RMU provide no detailed historical account beyond that association.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Umli culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Umitic","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Umitic</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Umli. In MERP it is their principal cultural tongue and coexists with Labba, Westron, and sometimes Khuzdul. The sources used by MERP-RMU provide no detailed historical account beyond that association.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Umli culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"RCfRaSZc3jyOJq9g"}
{"name":"Varadja","sort":320000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-varadja","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-varadja","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Varadja","pages":[{"name":"Varadja","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Varadja</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Langue des Variags de Khand dans le matériel MERP. Elle représente leur parler propre, employé aux côtés du Haradaic et du Westron dans les zones de contact. Le répertoire linguistique de référence l’identifie sans développer davantage son histoire.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Variag culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Varadja","pages":[{"name":"Varadja","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Varadja</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Variags of Khand in MERP material. It represents their own speech, used alongside Haradaic and Westron in contact regions. The reference language survey identifies it without further developing its history.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Variag culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Varadja","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Varadja</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The language of the Variags of Khand in MERP material. It represents their own speech, used alongside Haradaic and Westron in contact regions. The reference language survey identifies it without further developing its history.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Variag culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"S9ZVffw1A5vyLXI1"}
{"name":"Waildyth","sort":330000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-waildyth","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-waildyth","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Waildyth","pages":[{"name":"Waildyth","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Waildyth</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Développement MERP/ICE — langue signalée</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Système de signaux naturels des Béornides. Ses utilisateurs imitent ou modulent les bruits de la nature — cris d’animaux, vent et autres sons sauvages — afin de communiquer à distance sans révéler leur présence. Il ne possède aucune forme écrite. Dans RMU, Waildyth est donc traité comme une langue signalée plutôt que comme une langue parlée ou écrite ordinaire.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Beorning culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Waildyth","pages":[{"name":"Waildyth","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Waildyth</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development — signaled language</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A natural signaling system used by the Beornings. Users imitate or vary sounds of the wild—animal calls, wind, and other natural noises—to communicate over distance without revealing their presence. It has no written form. In RMU, Waildyth is therefore treated as a signaled language rather than an ordinary spoken or written tongue.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Beorning culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Waildyth","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Waildyth</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> MERP/ICE development — signaled language</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>A natural signaling system used by the Beornings. Users imitate or vary sounds of the wild—animal calls, wind, and other natural noises—to communicate over distance without revealing their presence. It has no written form. In RMU, Waildyth is therefore treated as a signaled language rather than an ordinary spoken or written tongue.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>MERP Beorning culture</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"pMiGKx2ArTCdeL0q"}
{"name":"Westron","sort":340000,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"collection":"merp-rmu-rules","key":"langage-westron","section":"langages","compendiumSourceKey":"langage-westron","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-languages","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"regles-langages","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Westron","pages":[{"name":"Westron","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Westron</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Statut :</strong> Tolkien / compléments MERP</p></section><h2>Présentation</h2><p>Le Parler Commun est la grande langue véhiculaire de l’ouest de la Terre du Milieu au Troisième Âge. Il est employé par des populations très diverses comme langue commune, avec de nombreux accents et dialectes régionaux. Il descend historiquement de l’Adúnaic et des contacts avec les langues des peuples de la Terre du Milieu. Dans la fiction éditoriale du Seigneur des Anneaux, le texte anglais représente en grande partie le Westron traduit.</p><h2>Usage dans MERP-RMU</h2><p>Cette notice est descriptive. Les rangs linguistiques effectifs d’un personnage sont gérés par les compétences RMU <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em> et <em>Language Signaled</em> selon les données de sa Culture.</p><h2>Sources éditoriales</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Translating Tolkien</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]},"en":{"name":"Westron","pages":[{"name":"Westron","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Westron</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP additions</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The Common Speech is the great lingua franca of western Middle-earth in the Third Age. Many different peoples use it as a shared language, with numerous regional accents and dialects. It descends historically from Adûnaic and from contact with the languages of Middle-earth. Within the translation conceit of The Lord of the Rings, much of the English text represents translated Westron.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Translating Tolkien</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}]}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"pages":[{"name":"Westron","text":{"content":"<div class=\"merp-rmu-rules merp-rmu-language-entry\"><h1>Westron</h1><section class=\"merp-rmu-rule-summary\"><p><strong>Status :</strong> Tolkien / MERP additions</p></section><h2>Overview</h2><p>The Common Speech is the great lingua franca of western Middle-earth in the Third Age. Many different peoples use it as a shared language, with numerous regional accents and dialects. It descends historically from Adûnaic and from contact with the languages of Middle-earth. Within the translation conceit of The Lord of the Rings, much of the English text represents translated Westron.</p><h2>Use in MERP-RMU</h2><p>This entry is descriptive. A character’s actual language ranks are handled through the RMU skills <em>Language Spoken</em>, <em>Language Written</em>, <em>Lip Reading</em>, and <em>Language Signaled</em> according to Culture data.</p><h2>Editorial sources</h2><ul><li>RMSS/RMFRP pp. 218–219</li><li>Tolkien Estate — Translating Tolkien</li></ul></div>"},"title":{"show":false}}],"_id":"9K6Wv5gsBghlpbvW"}
